<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Three ET Cons mines hit by strike.</title>
<headline>Three ET Cons mines hit by strike.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's National Union of Mineworkers said on Monday that about 2,000 mineworkers at three of Avgold Ltd's Eastern Transvaal Consolidated Mines Ltd had gone on strike.  </p>
<p>The union said the strike had been sparked by &quot;mine management intransigence&quot; and a &quot;lack of sensitivity&quot; on an issue involving a hostel manager, against whom the union had laid charges of fraud.</p>
<p>It accused the hostel manager of corruption and of breaching the workers' code of conduct.</p>
<p>It said that despite various options to resolve the issue, no solution could be reached. The union added that its officials would meet mine management on Monday afternoon.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
